course: dictionary
lesson: 9101
title: Small: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Small is a short word with many meanings, and the words around it show you which one to use. Most often it means little in size: «Birds may nest in a nest box in spring, and a small hole keeps out bigger birds.» Here the hole is narrow, so small means little in size.
explain: Small can also mean little in number or amount, or not important. «Even a small rise warms the planet» means a little rise still has a big effect. «Proofreading means hunting the small slips» means tiny mistakes like a wrong spelling. Ask yourself: is it talking about size, number, or importance?
explain: Small can mean young, as in «when I was small», and it can mean mean or unkind, as in «That was a small thing to do». Smaller means less big than another one, and smallest means less big than all the others. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: Small means little in size, number, amount or importance.
fact: Smaller means less big than another one; smallest means less big than all the others.
fact: «Small» can also mean mean or petty, as in «That was a small thing to do», which means it was unkind.
fact: In maths, you «subtract the smaller number from the bigger one», so smaller is used to compare two numbers.
fact: In exam writing, small can be replaced by formal words such as minimal (as little as possible) and negligible (so small it hardly matters).
exercise: «Birds may nest in a nest box in spring, and a small hole keeps out bigger birds.» What does small mean here? | Not important | Young | Kind | *Little in size
exercise: «That was a small thing to do when she took his pencil.» What does small mean here? | Young | Little in size | *Mean or unkind | Not important
exercise: In maths, which word means less big than all the others? | *Smallest | Bigger | Largest | Smaller
test: «Even a small rise warms the planet.» In this sentence, small means | Mean or unkind | Young | Smallest of all | *Little in amount
test: Which meaning fits «when I was small»? | *Young | Not important | Narrow | Little in number
exam: Which formal word could replace small in «a small effect on the results»? | Ordinary | Enormous | *Negligible | Loud
